in{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|)+2(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =5(0-(6\\cdot (-4)-1\\cdot 2)+0)+2(0-(3\\cdot (-4)-1\\cdot (-3))+0) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 26+2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =130+18 \\\\  & =148\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-36053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "055b3809-f9aa-5dcc-8c1a-b0eb71020d7e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32800"] :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+8\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =8{C}_{12} \\\\  & =8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & 8 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ -1 & ∗ & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & ∗ & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-8((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =8(6\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2)-0+0 \\\\  & =8\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =112\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4447"] :question/problem "